# item27j: Banque01 story route. Follows the map's own cutscene flow by player input; there are
# no `set_goal` bridges. Objective 0 "Access the strongroom." must complete through the game's own
# chain (Cine1 teller scene -> Cine15 Jones scene -> `event fin_flash` -> XIIIDispatcher4 ->
# GT_quitterbanque -> XIIIGoalTrigger0), which promotes objective 1, and objective 1 "Escape from
# the bank." completes through Cine11's `playerevent fin_map` -> XIIIGoalTrigger2 (GoalNumber 1)
# -> DoTravel -> Amos01.
#
# Two measured VM blockers stall that flow (probes in local/re/item27j/, report
# local/reports/item27j-banque-route.md):
#   - VM blocker 1: Cine1's `movseqb w 13 w 14 w 16 w 63` (action[46], from t=38.5) never moves the
#     teller past the armored door the player opened (`playerevent porteblindee1`, action[39]): the
#     pawn's move is rejected by a door-panel brush at x=-1600.9 (hit normal [1,0,0]) even though
#     the same door lets the player through after the event. Cine1 therefore never reaches its
#     `event toto` (action[59]) that unlocks Porte8, and `use Porte8` stays "Locked" (measured).
#   - VM blocker 2: Cine15's `movseqb sp 0.25 w 33 w 34` (action[20]) is rejected at hit_time=0.0
#     (normal [0,0.994,0.112]) on every steering step at Jones's own position (-7142,-1974), so
#     `event fin_flash` (action[45]) never fires, objective 0 never completes and no travel is
#     requested. The player teleported to the same spot walks freely in all directions, so the
#     block is specific to the pawn's taller move box (extent [34,34,75]).
# The route still performs every player-reachable step of the flow so the run exercises as much of
# the game's own chain as the VM allows; where the flow is stalled the route continues with
# labelled diagnostic teleports and records the stalled state in the log.
#
# Teleport classes used below:
#   - "flow touch": teleport onto a trigger volume the flow depends on; the run delivers the
#     volume's own engine `Touch`, so every touch is the game's own code.
#   - "measured recipe": the D->E re-entry around DetectionVolume1. Banque0's STA_DonneCle tick
#     released `recoit_cle` 0.1 s after the player RE-ENTERED DV1 in every probe that used it, and
#     never while the player sat inside from the start (mechanism unresolved; measured probes 2-5).
#   - "movement gap": a labelled teleport across an obstacle the flow opens but this VM cannot
#     (Porte8 locked by VM blocker 1; the strongroom approach has no verified walkable path).

# Leave the intro camera (WaitForFirstDisplay).
t=0.50 forward 1
t=1.50 forward 0

# Bank teller scene (Cine1): DetectionVolume1 (Event julien_cine) starts it through the game's own
# Touch. flow touch.
t=3.00 teleport -428 -2312 80

# Measured recipe: leave DV1 after Cine1's `event choatoi` (action[14], t=10.95) and re-enter, so
# Banque0's STA_DonneCle tick releases `recoit_cle` (arrives ~0.1 s after the re-entry touch) and
# Cine1 continues past `wait event recoit_cle` (action[16]).
t=11.00 teleport -544 -2183 80      # measured recipe: out of DV1 (no-fire spot D)
t=11.50 teleport -494 -2383 80      # measured recipe: re-enter DV1 -> recoit_cle

# The teller walks to the counter and opens the staff gate (fixed ~24 s of scene actions after
# recoit_cle; her `wait player 500`, action[32], passed with the player here in the probes).
t=23.00 teleport -540 -1350 80      # flow: within the teller's wait-player radius

# Cine1 `event james` (action[45]) starts Cine6 (James); his `wait player 700` (action[4]) needs
# the player this close for the dialogue, then `event ajulien` fires (unconsumed: Cine1 is stalled
# by VM blocker 1 at action[46]).
t=40.00 teleport -1760 -2480 -80    # flow: within James's wait-player radius

# Vault door Porte8: the flow unlocks it with the key via Cine1's `event toto`, which VM blocker 1
# prevents. The `use` below records the measured "Locked" state in the log.
t=44.00 teleport -2843 -6380 -150   # flow: to the vault door (armored door opened by Cine1[39])
t=45.00 use Porte8                  # diagnostic: measured "use Porte8: Locked" (VM blocker 1)
t=46.00 teleport -3000 -6300 -150   # movement gap: past locked Porte8 (key never granted)

# Strongroom: DetectionVolume12's Touch starts Cine15 (Jones). flow touch.
t=47.00 teleport -7616 -2784 1456   # flow touch: DetectionVolume12 (starts Cine15)
t=48.00 teleport -7142 -2100 880    # flow: within Jones's wait-player radii ([3] 300, [19] away 70)

# Cine15 plays its anims (~11 s), reaches `movseqb sp 0.25 w 33 w 34` (action[20]) and stalls there
# (VM blocker 2): `event fin_flash` (action[45]) never fires, so objective 0 cannot complete and
# objective 1 is never promoted. The run continues with the escape-flow volumes below so the log
# shows the route state when the 90 s budget ends.
t=55.00 teleport 1300.03 -1917.39 1478  # flow touch: TouchTrigger5 (Event vignracaille)
t=58.00 teleport 865 -4075 1530         # flow touch: TouchTrigger2 (Event arrivee_fbi)
t=61.00 teleport 1134 -4222 480         # flow touch: TouchTrigger3 (Event fbi_dial2)
t=64.00 teleport 1148 -4063 380         # flow touch: TouchTrigger4 (Event arrivee_amos)
t=67.00 teleport 1014.38 -4309 620      # flow touch: TouchTrigger10 (Event CarOut)
t=70.00 teleport 1341.37 -4019.51 380   # flow touch: XIIIGoalTrigger2 (Tag fin_map, GoalNumber 1)

# Wait for the game's own travel (Amos01 via the end-of-level chain). With VM blocker 2 the
# objective assertions in the route test fail before this matters.
t=73.00 wait_travel
